0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  B8Script interpreter for the Z80
0000                             ;  Spec: docs/b8script.md (2026-11-21).
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Three switches, set in the EQU lines below:
0000                             ;    CPM      0 = generic ROM build (KEY/CONOUT at fixed addresses)
0000                             ;             1 = CP/M 2.2 .COM file: loads the file named on the command line
0000                             ;    EDITOR   1 = with the line editor built in (see the end of this file):
0000                             ;                 the spec's suggested standard. It goes with either setting
0000                             ;                 of the other two.
0000                             ;    CHECKED  0 = no checks (spec: the programmer is responsible)
0000                             ;             1 = starts with every variable at 0 and every word undefined,
0000                             ;                 and stops on every error in the spec's table (and Ctrl-C)
0000                             ;                 with a four-line report: the letter and the place as line
0000                             ;                 and column, the text there, and both stacks. See `error`.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  In every build Ctrl-C stops a running program (an unchecked build stops
0000                             ;  without a word): see the console layer for the rules, the held key and
0000                             ;  the break-off cell.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Assembler: asm80 (https://maly.github.io/asm80-node/), Z80 mode.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                CPM:      EQU   0   ; 1 = CP/M .COM build
0000                CHECKED:   EQU   1   ; 1 = checked build
0000                EDITOR:   EQU   1   ; 1 = with the line editor
0000                EDGEN:    EQU   EDITOR*(1-CPM)   ; (the generic build with the editor)
0000                             ; (IF takes any value but 0 as true, so
0000                             ;  IF CHECKED+EDITOR means "either")
0000                TABP0:    EQU   EDGEN*(1-CHECKED)   ; (the build with its table in page zero)
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Register use, everywhere in the interpreter
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    BC   IP: the address of the next program character to read
0000                             ;    HL   TOS: the top data-stack cell is kept here, not in memory
0000                             ;    SP   the data stack: (SP) is NOS, the cell under TOS. The data stack is
0000                             ;         the Z80"s own stack, which is what the spec"s machine-code contract
0000                             ;         needs ("the data cells above the return address").
0000                             ;    HL'  return-stack pointer (the alternate HL). Entries are 2 bytes; the
0000                             ;         stack grows down. Only rpop and rpushn (and the checks) touch it.
0000                             ;    A DE scratch. Every handler is entered with HL = TOS and may use A, DE.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  One-byte calls. The routines used most are reached with RST, one byte
0000                             ;  instead of three:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RST 08h  rpop    pop the return stack into DE
0000                             ;    RST 18h  drop    drop TOS, then next character     (ends a handler)
0000                             ;    RST 20h  neg16   HL = -HL
0000                             ;    RST 28h  putc    print A
0000                             ;    RST 30h  next    next character                    (ends a handler)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  RST 18h and RST 30h never return: an RST is a CALL, so the first thing
0000                             ;  each of them does is POP DE to throw the return address away.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The CP/M build can't own page zero, so the block from `vecs` to `vecend`
0000                             ;  (image addresses 0108h-0133h) is copied to 0008h-0033h when it starts. The
0000                             ;  code in that block is written to work at either place.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Dispatch. PTAB holds one byte per punctuation character: the low byte of
0000                             ;  its handler's address. The high byte is worked out from the character:
0000                             ;  the handlers of the first NPG1 characters (in code order) start in the
0000                             ;  image's second page, the rest in its first. The layout below keeps to
0000                             ;  that, and testing/chktab.py checks it in every build.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Memory map. Everything the interpreter writes is in four RAM pages:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RSPAGE   return stack, 112 entries (the pointer stays inside this page)
0000                             ;    DSPAGE   data stack, 127 cells (the top four bytes of the page are spare,
0000                             ;             so a full stack runs two bytes into the page below)
0000                             ;    LETPAGE  letter cells: A..Z at +00h..+33h, a..z at +40h..+73h (so a word
0000                             ;             cell is always 64 bytes below its variable), the heap pointer at
0000                             ;             +7Ch, interpreter variables in the gaps, and the -n? line buffer
0000                             ;             at +80h..+FFh
0000                             ;    PROG     the program text, NUL-terminated; the heap starts after the NUL
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The stacks sit below the letter page, so "the program's own space" (what
0000                             ;  the checked build lets ! and . write) is the single range from the letter
0000                             ;  page up to the heap limit. Each stack has a guard band: the data stack can
0000                             ;  overrun by a cell or two (and the calls made while it is full, the error
0000                             ;  report's included) into the top 32 bytes of the return-stack page, which
0000                             ;  are never used, and the return stack by one entry into the page below it.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                          IF   CPM   
                    BDOS:     EQU   0005h   
                    BASE:     EQU   0100h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   CPM*(1-EDITOR)   
                    EXIT:     EQU   0000h   ; warm boot
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IFN   CPM   
0000                             ; ---- generic machine: edit these to suit -----------------------------------
0000                KEY:      EQU   0FF06h   ; a waiting key in A, or A = 0 if none is
0000                             ;   waiting. The zero flag must match A
0000                             ;   (end the routine with OR A / RET).
0000                CONOUT:   EQU   0FF03h   ; print the character in A
0000                             ;   KEY and CONOUT must preserve BC, DE, HL and HL'.
0000                RSPAGE:   EQU   80h   ; 8000h return stack
0000                DSPAGE:   EQU   81h   ; 8100h data stack
0000                LETPAGE:   EQU   82h   ; 8200h letter cells and line buffer
0000                PROG:     EQU   8300h   ; where the loader puts the program text
0000                HEAPLIM:   EQU   0F0h   ; the heap must stay below F000h (a page)
0000                BASE:     EQU   0000h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    EXIT:     EQU   0FF09h   ; where to go when the program ends
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDGEN   
0000                LEAVE:    EQU   0FF09h   ; where the editor's ^X goes
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDITOR*CPM   
                    LEAVE:    EQU   0000h   ; the editor's ^X: warm boot
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDITOR   
0000                EXIT:     EQU   edend   ; a program that ends goes back to the editor,
0000                SKEND:    EQU   skend   ;   also when it ends inside skip
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   1-EDITOR   
                    SKEND:    EQU   EXIT   
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                MSLOOP:   EQU   40   ; n? inner loop count for about 1 ms (1-255):
0000                             ; each pass calls getk once, so tune it for
0000                             ; your clock and your KEY routine. (The wait
0000                             ; for a second Ctrl-C uses it too: 250 ms.)
0000                             ; letter-page layout (offsets inside LETPAGE)
0000                LET:      EQU   LETPAGE*256   
0000                HEAP:     EQU   LET+7Ch   ; the heap pointer
0000                RSAVE:    EQU   LET+34h   ; gap after Z: return stack pointer, saved
0000                             ;   around machine code;
0000                NPEND:    EQU   LET+38h   ;   minus the address of the program's end
0000                             ;   (the heap"s first byte), for the checked "_';
0000                EDLN:     EQU   LET+3Ah   ;   the editor: the number of the line that ^E
0000                             ;   put in the input line (0: none)
0000                KEYBUF:   EQU   LET+7Ah   ; gap after z: a key read by the break check and
0000                             ;   held for the next "?" (0: none);
0000                BRKOFF:   EQU   LET+7Bh   ;   the break-off cell: a program that stores a
0000                             ;   non-zero byte here gets Ctrl-C as a key
0000                LBHDR:    EQU   LET+7Eh   ; CP/M BDOS 10 header: max, count
0000                LINEBUF:   EQU   LET+80h   ; -n? text, ending in CR
0000                RSTOP:    EQU   RSPAGE*256+0E0h   ; empty return stack: the 32 bytes above it
0000                             ; take calls made while the data stack is full
0000                DSTOP:    EQU   DSPAGE*256+0FCh   ; empty data stack. The four bytes above it
0000                             ; are spare: a character can pop two cells
0000                             ; too many before the checked build sees it,
0000                             ; and the next call must not land on the
0000                             ; letter cells.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  The first 49 bytes: the entry, then the RST routines, with small handlers
0000                             ;  and routines filling the gaps between them. Generic: this IS page zero.
0000                             ;  CP/M: it is the start of the .COM file, and 0108h-0133h is also copied to
0000                             ;  page zero (see the header).
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                          .ORG   BASE   
0000                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                              XOR   A   ; 00  reset. (This byte, AFh, is also what an
0000                          ENDIF      ;     undefined word runs into: see e_hi.)
0000                          IF   1-EDGEN   
                              LD   SP,DSTOP   ; 00  reset, or the start of the .COM file
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*(1-CHECKED)   
                              LD   BC,PROG   ; 03  the IP
                              JR   st0   ; 06  (the rest of the startup is close by)
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                              JR   init   ; 04  (the rest of the startup is close by)
                              DW   0   ; 06  spare
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDGEN   
0000   AF                     XOR   A   ; 00  reset: no program yet. (This byte, AFh,
0001   32 00 83               LD   (PROG),A   ;     is also what an undefined word runs
0004   C3 6E 04               JP   init   ; 04  into in the checked build: see e_hi.)
0007   00                     NOP      ; 07  spare
0008                          ENDIF      
0008                          IF   CPM   
                              JP   start   ; 03
                              DW   0   ; 06  spare
0008                          ENDIF      
0008                VECS:        
0008                             ; ---- RST 08h: rpop: pop the return stack into DE ---------------------------
0008   D9           RPOP:     EXX      ; 08
0009   5E                     LD   E,(HL)   
000A   23                     INC   HL   
000B   56                     LD   D,(HL)   
000C   23                     INC   HL   
000D   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; across to the main registers
000E   D9                     EXX      
000F   D1                     POP   DE   
0010   C9                     RET      ; 10  (so RST 10h is not used)
0011                             ; ctl: the inner loop comes here for characters below 21h. A = c - 21h.
0011   C6 21        CTL:      ADD   A,21h   ; 11  back to c; zero only for NUL
0013   20 1C                  JR   NZ,next0   ;     the rest are ignored
0015   C3 B3 04     ENDPROG:   JP   EXIT   ;     the program has ended
0018                             ; ---- RST 18h: drop TOS, then next ------------------------------------------
0018   D1           RST18:    POP   DE   ; 18  discard the RST's return address
0019   E1                     POP   HL   ;     new TOS = NOS
001A   18 15                  JR   nx   
001C   E5           H_FROMR:   PUSH   HL   ; 1C  "}" return stack to TOS
001D   CF                     RST   08h   
001E   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
001F   F7                     RST   30h   
0020                             ; ---- RST 20h: neg16: HL = -HL (keeps BC, DE) -------------------------------
0020   AF           NEG16:    XOR   A   ; 20
0021   95                     SUB   L   
0022   6F                     LD   L,A   
0023   9F                     SBC   A,A   
0024   94                     SUB   H   
0025   67                     LD   H,A   
0026   C9                     RET      
0027   00                     NOP      ; 27  spare
0028                             ; ---- RST 28h: putc: print A (keeps BC, DE, HL, HL') ------------------------
0028                RST28:       
0028                          IFN   CPM   
0028   C3 03 FF     PUTC:     JP   CONOUT   ; 28
002B                          ENDIF      
002B                          IF   CPM   
                              JP   putc   ; 28
002B                          ENDIF      
002B   E9           JPHL:     JP   (HL)   ; 2B  (for the machine-code call)
002C   E3           H_TOR:    EX   (SP),HL   ; 2C  "{" TOS to the return stack: the new TOS
002D   C3 B7 00               JP   rpushn   ;     comes up, the old one goes across
0030                             ; ---- RST 30h: next character -----------------------------------------------
0030   D1           RST30:    POP   DE   ; 30  discard the RST's return address
0031                NX:          
0031                          IF   CPM   
                              JP   next0   ; (this copy runs in page zero)
0031                          ENDIF      
0031                VECEND:      
0031                             ; =============================================================================
0031                             ;  The inner loop: read one character and sort it by range.
0031                             ; 
0031                             ;    00h          end of program
0031                             ;    01h-20h, 7Fh-FFh   ignored (control, space, DEL, high bytes)
0031                             ;    30h-39h      digit: read a whole number
0031                             ;    41h-5Ah      A-Z: call the word in that letter's cell
0031                             ;    61h-7Ah      a-z: push the address of that letter's cell
0031                             ;    the rest     punctuation: jump through PTAB, 32 entries, in code order
0031                             ; =============================================================================
0031                NEXT0:       
0031                          IF   CHECKED   
0031   CD 1D 03               CALL   chkstk   ; both stacks are checked once per character
0034                          ENDIF      
0034   0A                     LD   A,(BC)   
0035   03                     INC   BC   
0036   D6 21                  SUB   21h   ; A = c - 21h
0038   38 D7                  JR   C,ctl   ; c < 21h: NUL ends, the rest are ignored
003A   FE 0F                  CP   0Fh   
003C   38 25                  JR   C,punct   ; 21h-2Fh: PTAB index 0-14
003E   D6 0F                  SUB   0Fh   ; A = c - 30h
0040   FE 0A                  CP   0Ah   
0042   38 5D                  JR   C,digit   ; 30h-39h
0044   FE 11                  CP   11h   
0046   38 19                  JR   C,p3a   ; 3Ah-40h
0048   D6 11                  SUB   11h   ; A = c - 41h
004A   FE 1A                  CP   1Ah   
004C   38 5F                  JR   C,upper   ; 41h-5Ah: A = letter index 0-25
004E   FE 20                  CP   20h   
0050   38 0D                  JR   C,p5b   ; 5Bh-60h
0052   FE 3A                  CP   3Ah   
0054   38 51                  JR   C,lower   ; 61h-7Ah: A = 20h-39h (cell +64 bytes)
0056   FE 3E                  CP   3Eh   
0058                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              JR   NC,next0   ; 7Fh-FFh: ignored
0058                          ENDIF      
0058                          IF   CHECKED   
0058   28 D7                  JR   Z,next0   ; 7Fh, DEL: ignored
005A   D2 49 03               JP   NC,e_hi   ; 80h-FFh: reserved
005D                          ENDIF      
005D   D6 1A                  SUB   1Ah   ; 7Bh-7Eh: -1Eh in all, index 28-31
005F   D6 09        P5B:      SUB   9   ; 5Bh-60h: -4 in all, index 22-27
0061   C6 05        P3A:      ADD   A,5   ; 3Ah-40h: index 15-21
0063                .macro PTABLE,
0063                             ; 
0063                 DB      h_store & 0FFh  ; !
0063                 DB      h_str & 0FFh    ; "
0063                 DB      h_num & 0FFh    ; #
0063                 DB      h_print & 0FFh  ; $
0063                 DB      h_swap & 0FFh   ; %
0063                 DB      h_and & 0FFh    ; &
0063                 DB      h_emit & 0FFh   ; '
0063                 DB      h_open & 0FFh   ; (
0063                 DB      h_close & 0FFh  ; )
0063                 DB      h_mul & 0FFh    ; *
0063                 DB      h_add & 0FFh    ; +
0063                 DB      h_cfetch & 0FFh ; ,
0063                 DB      h_sub & 0FFh    ; -
0063                 DB      h_cstore & 0FFh ; .
0063                 DB      h_div & 0FFh    ; /
0063                 DB      h_dup & 0FFh    ; :
0063                 DB      h_drop & 0FFh   ; ;
0063                 DB      h_lt & 0FFh     ; <
0063                 DB      h_eq & 0FFh     ; =
0063                 DB      h_gt & 0FFh     ; >
0063                 DB      h_key & 0FFh    ; ?
0063                 DB      h_fetch & 0FFh  ; @
0063                 DB      h_def & 0FFh    ; [
0063                 DB      h_break & 0FFh  ; \
0063                 DB      h_ret & 0FFh    ; ]
0063                 DB      h_xor & 0FFh    ; ^
0063                 DB      h_alloc & 0FFh  ; _
0063                 DB      h_grave & 0FFh  ; `
0063                 DB      h_tor & 0FFh    ; {
0063                 DB      h_or & 0FFh     ; |
0063                 DB      h_fromr & 0FFh  ; }
0063                 DB      h_not & 0FFh    ; ~
0063                .endm
0063                 
0063                             ; Punctuation: A = the PTAB index. The handler starts with HL = TOS,
0063                             ; untouched, and A, DE free.
0063   C6 AD        PUNCT:    ADD   A,PTAB & 0FFh   ; PTAB never crosses a page
0065   5F                     LD   E,A   
0066   16 02                  LD   D,PTAB / 256   ; (0 if the table is in page zero)
0068   FE C3                  CP   (PTAB & 0FFh) + NPG1   ; carry: one of the first NPG1
006A   1A                     LD   A,(DE)   
006B   5F                     LD   E,A   ; the handler's low byte
006C                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-TABP0)   
006C   16 00                  LD   D,0   
006E                          ENDIF      
006E                          IFN   CPM   
006E   CB 12                  RL   D   ; its page: 0 + carry
0070                          ENDIF      
0070                          IF   CPM   
                              LD   D,1   
                              JR   NC,pu1   
                              INC   D   ; its page: 1 + carry
                    PU1:         
0070                          ENDIF      
0070   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; jump to it; the stack is balanced again
0071   C9                     RET      ;   when the handler starts
0072                             ; The rest of the startup: here so that the generic reset code can reach it
0072                             ; with JR. st0: find the program's NUL; the heap starts after it.
0072                             ; (The editor build has its own copy of this, next to the editor.)
0072                             ; A checked build first clears the lower half of the letter page (A = 0):
0072                             ; every variable starts at 0, every word cell holds 0000h, the address an
0072                             ; undefined word is caught at (see e_hi), and no key is held back.
0072                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                    INIT:     LD   HL,LET   
                    INI1:     LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   L   
                              JP   P,ini1   ; +00h to +7Fh
                              LD   BC,PROG   ; the IP
0072                          ENDIF      
0072                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    ST0:      LD   H,B   
                              LD   L,C   
                              XOR   A   
                    ST1:      CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   NZ,st1   
0072                          ENDIF      
0072                          IF   1-EDITOR   
                    ST2:      LD   (HEAP),HL   
0072                          ENDIF      
0072                          IF   CHECKED*(1-EDITOR)   
                              RST   20h   ; minus the heap"s first address: "_' may not
                              LD   (NPEND),HL   ;   release below it
0072                          ENDIF      
0072                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)*(1-CPM)   
                              LD   H,A   ; (A = 0) no key is held, and the break key
                              LD   L,A   ;   is on (the checked build has cleared
0072                          ENDIF      ;   these)
0072                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)*CPM   
                              LD   HL,0   
0072                          ENDIF      
0072                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)   
                              LD   (KEYBUF),HL   
0072                          ENDIF      
0072                          IF   1-EDITOR   
                              EXX      
                              LD   HL,RSTOP   ; the return stack is empty
                              EXX      
                              RST   30h   ; (its return address is thrown away)
0072                          ENDIF      
0072                             ; In the unchecked generic editor build the table is here, in the first
0072                             ; page, which saves loading D twice. (The other builds have no room for it
0072                             ; here: theirs is further down.)
0072                          IF   TABP0   
                    PTAB:        
                              ;*Macro unroll:  PTABLE
                              DB   h_store & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_str & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_num & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_print & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_swap & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_and & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_emit & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_open & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_close & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_mul & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_add & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_cfetch & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_sub & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_cstore & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_div & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_dup & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_drop & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_lt & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_eq & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_gt & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_key & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_fetch & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_def & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_break & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_ret & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_xor & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_alloc & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_grave & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_tor & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_or & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_fromr & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_not & 0FFh   
                    PTABEND:      
0072                          ENDIF      
0072                             ; =============================================================================
0072                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's first page: ^ _ ` | ~
0072                             ;  (00bbIGFuZCA= are up among the RST routines.) The machine-code call, exec,
0072                             ;  is here too: it belongs to "`" and makes the page come out right.
0072                             ; =============================================================================
0072   D1           H_XOR:    POP   DE   
0073   7C                     LD   A,H   
0074   AA                     XOR   D   
0075   67                     LD   H,A   
0076   7D                     LD   A,L   
0077   AB                     XOR   E   
0078   6F                     LD   L,A   
0079   F7                     RST   30h   
007A   D1           H_OR:     POP   DE   
007B   7C                     LD   A,H   
007C   B2                     OR   D   
007D   67                     LD   H,A   
007E   7D                     LD   A,L   
007F   B3                     OR   E   
0080   6F                     LD   L,A   
0081   F7                     RST   30h   
0082   E7           H_NOT:    RST   20h   ; ~x = -x - 1
0083   2B                     DEC   HL   
0084   F7                     RST   30h   
0085                             ; "_" ( n -- addr ): the heap pointer moves by n, a signed count (the add is
0085                             ; the same either way); TOS is the old pointer.
0085   ED 5B 7C 82  H_ALLOC:   LD   DE,(HEAP)   
0089                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
                              LD   A,H   ; the count's sign, for chkhp
0089                          ENDIF      
0089   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ; the new top
008A                          IF   CHECKED   
008A   CD 53 03               CALL   chkhp   
008D                          ENDIF      
008D   22 7C 82               LD   (HEAP),HL   
0090   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0091   F7                     RST   30h   
0092   D9           EXEC:     EXX      
0093   22 34 82               LD   (RSAVE),HL   ; machine code may change the alternates
0096   D9                     EXX      
0097   CD 2B 00               CALL   jphl   
009A   D9                     EXX      
009B   2A 34 82               LD   HL,(RSAVE)   
009E   D9                     EXX      
009F   E1                     POP   HL   
00A0   F7                     RST   30h   
00A1                             ; ---- the letters and digits (here, in the middle, so that the inner loop's
00A1                             ; ---- short jumps reach them, and the handlers after them reach rpushn) ------
00A1                             ; Digits: step back onto the first digit and read the whole number.
00A1   E5           DIGIT:    PUSH   HL   
00A2   0B                     DEC   BC   
00A3   CD 2F 02               CALL   rdnum   
00A6   F7                     RST   30h   
00A7                             ; a-z: push the cell's address (the cell is the variable)
00A7   E5           LOWER:    PUSH   HL   
00A8   87                     ADD   A,A   
00A9   6F                     LD   L,A   
00AA   26 82                  LD   H,LETPAGE   
00AC   F7                     RST   30h   
00AD                             ; A-Z: call the word. The return address (the IP after the letter) goes on
00AD                             ; the return stack, and the IP becomes the address in the letter's cell.
00AD   C5           UPPER:    PUSH   BC   ; the return address, for rpushn
00AE   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; park TOS
00AF   87                     ADD   A,A   
00B0   6F                     LD   L,A   
00B1   26 82                  LD   H,LETPAGE   ; HL -> cell
00B3   4E                     LD   C,(HL)   
00B4   2C                     INC   L   
00B5   46                     LD   B,(HL)   ; IP = the word's body
00B6   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; TOS back, and fall into rpushn
00B7                             ; rpushn: move the top cell of the data stack (in memory) to the return
00B7                             ; stack, then next. Everything that pushes the return stack ends here.
00B7                             ; 
00B7                             ; The break key is looked at here, so at every word call and loop-back (and
00B7                             ; block entry and "{"), but only one time in 256: B', which nothing else
00B7                             ; uses, counts them. Reading the keyboard can be slow (it is a BDOS call
00B7                             ; under CP/M), and this way it costs a loop four bytes and 14 T-states.
00B7                             ; (DEC B, not DJNZ: its zero flag lasts through the EXX, so one EXX serves
00B7                             ; both ways out.)
00B7   D9           RPUSHN:   EXX      
00B8   D1                     POP   DE   
00B9   2B                     DEC   HL   
00BA   72                     LD   (HL),D   
00BB   2B                     DEC   HL   
00BC   73                     LD   (HL),E   
00BD   05                     DEC   B   
00BE   D9                     EXX      
00BF   CC DF 02               CALL   Z,pollk   
00C2   F7                     RST   30h   
00C3                             ; ---- machine code: the grave -----------------------------------------------
00C3                             ; "`" plus a hex digit loads bytes: ( addr -- addr' ). Pairs of hex digits
00C3                             ; are stored from addr until a non-hex character; then a RET (C9h) is
00C3                             ; written and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
00C3                             ; "`" plus anything else calls the machine code at TOS: ( addr -- ). The
00C3                             ; code is entered by CALL with the data stack above the return address; it
00C3                             ; must keep BC, and on return the top cell becomes the new TOS.
00C3   CD CD 02     H_GRAVE:   CALL   hexc   
00C6   30 CA                  JR   NC,exec   
00C8   77           HX1:      LD   (HL),A   ; the high digit goes in first ...
00C9   CD CD 02               CALL   hexc   
00CC   30 08                  JR   NC,hx2   ; odd digit: consumed, and the RET below
00CE   ED 6F                  RLD      ;   overwrites it
00D0   23                     INC   HL   ; ... and RLD shifts it up under the low one
00D1   CD CD 02               CALL   hexc   
00D4   38 F2                  JR   C,hx1   
00D6   36 C9        HX2:      LD   (HL),0C9h   ; (never range-checked: the spec says so)
00D8   F7                     RST   30h   
00D9                             ; ---- where the two pages meet ----------------------------------------------
00D9                             ; The first page ends somewhere among the next four handlers, ] \ [ @ (they
00D9                             ; are in falling code order for this), and where exactly differs between the
00D9                             ; builds: NPG1 follows. Every handler below these four must start in the
00D9                             ; second page, and every one above in the first; chktab.py checks both.
00D9                             ; "]" returns: pop an address and jump to it.
00D9   CF           H_RET:    RST   08h   
00DA   42                     LD   B,D   
00DB   4B                     LD   C,E   
00DC   F7           BRK1:     RST   30h   
00DD                             ; "\" ( flag -- ): true skips to the next ")" or "]" at this level; ")"
00DD                             ; drops the block start, "]" returns. No closer at all ends the program.
00DD   7C           H_BREAK:   LD   A,H   
00DE   B5                     OR   L   
00DF   E1                     POP   HL   
00E0   28 FA                  JR   Z,brk1   
00E2   CD 56 02               CALL   skip   
00E5   B7                     OR   A   ; skip returns 0 for ")"
00E6   20 F1                  JR   NZ,h_ret   
00E8   CF           RDROP:    RST   08h   
00E9   F7                     RST   30h   
00EA                             ; "[" followed by a letter stores the body"s address in that letter"s cell:
00EA                             ; uppercase is a word, lowercase a variable. Followed by a space it pushes
00EA                             ; the body"s address instead. Either way it then skips to the matching "]'.
00EA                             ; (The unchecked build takes anything that is not a letter as the space; the
00EA                             ; checked build stops on it.)
00EA   0A           H_DEF:    LD   A,(BC)   
00EB   03                     INC   BC   
00EC   D6 41                  SUB   "A"   ; a letter gives 0-25 or 32-57: lowercase
00EE   5F                     LD   E,A   ;   lands 64 bytes up
00EF   E6 DF                  AND   0DFh   ; fold case
00F1   FE 1A                  CP   26   
00F3   30 0B                  JR   NC,def2   ; not a letter
00F5   CB 23                  SLA   E   
00F7   16 82                  LD   D,LETPAGE   ; DE -> cell
00F9   79                     LD   A,C   
00FA   12                     LD   (DE),A   
00FB   1C                     INC   E   
00FC   78                     LD   A,B   
00FD   12                     LD   (DE),A   
00FE   18 09                  JR   skipnx   
0100                DEF2:        
0100                          IF   CHECKED   
0100   7B                     LD   A,E   
0101   FE DF                  CP   " "-"A"+256   
0103   C2 85 03               JP   NZ,e_brack   ; anything but a letter or a space
0106                          ENDIF      
0106   E5                     PUSH   HL   ; an anonymous block: push its address
0107   60                     LD   H,B   
0108   69                     LD   L,C   
0109                SKIPNX:      
0109                          IF   CHECKED   
0109   0B                     DEC   BC   ; back onto the letter, so that skip finds its
010A                          ENDIF      ;   opener, the "[", just before where it starts
010A   CD 56 02     SKIPO:    CALL   skip   
010D   F7                     RST   30h   
010E   5E           H_FETCH:   LD   E,(HL)   ; "@"
010F   23                     INC   HL   
0110   56                     LD   D,(HL)   
0111   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0112   F7                     RST   30h   
0113                             ; =============================================================================
0113                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's second page.
0113                             ;  "?" is the last (with "," inside it), so its long tail may run past that
0113                             ;  page.
0113                             ; =============================================================================
0113                             ; "(" ( flag -- ): true pushes the block start and enters; false skips to
0113                             ; the matching ")".
0113   7C           H_OPEN:   LD   A,H   
0114   B5                     OR   L   
0115   E1                     POP   HL   
0116   28 F2                  JR   Z,skipo   
0118   C5                     PUSH   BC   ; the block starts at the IP
0119   18 9C                  JR   rpushn   
011B                             ; ")" ( flag -- ): true jumps back to the block start (and keeps it); false
011B                             ; drops it and carries on.
011B   7C           H_CLOSE:   LD   A,H   
011C   B5                     OR   L   
011D   E1                     POP   HL   
011E   28 C8                  JR   Z,rdrop   
0120   CF                     RST   08h   ; pop the block start ...
0121   42                     LD   B,D   
0122   4B                     LD   C,E   
0123   C5                     PUSH   BC   
0124   18 91                  JR   rpushn   ; ... and push it back
0126                             ; ---- arithmetic and logic: ( NOS TOS -- result ) ---------------------------
0126                             ; "-" has two jobs: directly before a digit it starts a negative number.
0126   0A           H_SUB:    LD   A,(BC)   
0127   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
0129   FE 0A                  CP   10   
012B   38 04                  JR   C,negnum   
012D   E7                     RST   20h   ; a - b = a + (-b): fall into "+"
012E   D1           H_ADD:    POP   DE   
012F   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
0130   F7                     RST   30h   
0131   E5           NEGNUM:   PUSH   HL   ; a negative number: read it, negate it
0132   CD 2F 02               CALL   rdnum   
0135   E7                     RST   20h   
0136   F7                     RST   30h   
0137   D1           H_AND:    POP   DE   
0138   7C                     LD   A,H   
0139   A2                     AND   D   
013A   67                     LD   H,A   
013B   7D                     LD   A,L   
013C   A3                     AND   E   
013D   6F                     LD   L,A   
013E   F7                     RST   30h   
013F                             ; Signed compares. Both are "HL < DE" for the right pair: "<" swaps the two
013F                             ; cells first. Flipping both sign bits turns a signed compare into an
013F                             ; unsigned one (and XOR clears the carry for SBC); SBC HL,HL then turns the
013F                             ; carry into -1 or 0 with no branch.
013F   E3           H_LT:     EX   (SP),HL   ; a < b: HL = a, and b is popped next
0140   D1           H_GT:     POP   DE   ; a > b  is  b < a: HL = b, DE = a
0141   7C                     LD   A,H   
0142   EE 80                  XOR   80h   
0144   67                     LD   H,A   
0145   7A                     LD   A,D   
0146   EE 80                  XOR   80h   
0148   57                     LD   D,A   
0149   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   ; carry if HL < DE
014B   ED 62        TF:       SBC   HL,HL   ; carry -> -1 or 0
014D   F7                     RST   30h   
014E   D1           H_EQ:     POP   DE   
014F   B7                     OR   A   
0150   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   
0152   7C                     LD   A,H   
0153   B5                     OR   L   
0154   FE 01                  CP   1   ; carry only if a - b = 0
0156   18 F3                  JR   tf   
0158                             ; "*": shift-and-add, 16 rounds; only the low 16 bits are kept. The
0158                             ; multiplier shifts up through A:C.
0158   D1           H_MUL:    POP   DE   ; DE = multiplicand
0159   C5                     PUSH   BC   
015A   7C                     LD   A,H   
015B   4D                     LD   C,L   ; A:C = multiplier
015C   21 00 00               LD   HL,0   
015F   06 10                  LD   B,16   
0161   29           MUL1:     ADD   HL,HL   
0162   CB 21                  SLA   C   
0164   17                     RLA      
0165   30 01                  JR   NC,mul2   
0167   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
0168   10 F7        MUL2:     DJNZ   mul1   
016A   C1                     POP   BC   
016B   F7                     RST   30h   
016C                             ; "/" ( a b -- q r ): the remainder is on top. Truncates toward zero; r takes
016C                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b and r the sign
016C                             ; of a. Dividing by zero returns two cells of no meaning; the checked build
016C                             ; stops on it.
016C                H_DIV:       
016C                          IF   CHECKED   
016C   7C                     LD   A,H   
016D   B5                     OR   L   
016E   CA 82 03               JP   Z,e_zero   
0171                          ENDIF      
0171   D1                     POP   DE   ; DE = a, HL = b
0172   C5                     PUSH   BC   ; free BC for udiv
0173   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; a, for r's sign
0174   7A                     LD   A,D   
0175   AC                     XOR   H   
0176   F5                     PUSH   AF   ; S flag = sign of q
0177   CB 7C                  BIT   7,H   
0179   C4 20 00               CALL   NZ,neg16   ; HL = |b|
017C   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
017D   CB 7C                  BIT   7,H   
017F   C4 20 00               CALL   NZ,neg16   ; HL = |a|, DE = |b|
0182   CD 09 02               CALL   udiv   ; HL = q, DE = r
0185   F1                     POP   AF   
0186   FC 20 00               CALL   M,neg16   ; q's sign
0189   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; HL = r, DE = q
018A   F1                     POP   AF   ; A = a's high byte
018B   B7                     OR   A   
018C   FC 20 00               CALL   M,neg16   ; r's sign
018F   C1                     POP   BC   
0190   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; q under r
0191   F7                     RST   30h   
0192                             ; ---- stack and storage -----------------------------------------------------
0192   E5           H_DUP:    PUSH   HL   ; ":"
0193   F7                     RST   30h   
0194   E3           H_SWAP:   EX   (SP),HL   ; "%"
0195   F7                     RST   30h   
0196                             ; (The checked build tests the address before it takes the value off the
0196                             ; stack, so that an error report shows both.)
0196                H_CSTORE:      ; "." ( c addr -- )
0196                          IF   CHECKED   
0196   CD 68 03               CALL   chkst   
0199                          ENDIF      
0199   D1                     POP   DE   
019A   73                     LD   (HL),E   
019B   DF           H_DROP:   RST   18h   ; ";" is this one byte
019C                H_STORE:      ; "!" ( n addr -- )
019C                          IF   CHECKED   
019C   CD 68 03               CALL   chkst   
019F                          ENDIF      
019F   D1                     POP   DE   
01A0   73                     LD   (HL),E   
01A1   23                     INC   HL   
01A2   72                     LD   (HL),D   
01A3   DF                     RST   18h   
01A4                             ; ---- console ---------------------------------------------------------------
01A4                             ; 22h pushes the address of the text after it and skips the string.
01A4   E5           H_STR:    PUSH   HL   
01A5   60                     LD   H,B   
01A6   69                     LD   L,C   
01A7   CD 45 02               CALL   skipstr   
01AA                          IF   CHECKED   
01AA   B7                     OR   A   ; 0: the text ran out before the closing quote
01AB   CA 7A 03               JP   Z,e_quote   
01AE                          ENDIF      
01AE   F7                     RST   30h   
01AF                             ; "$" prints the string at TOS, decoding escapes: "/" plus a character
01AF                             ; clears that character"s bit 6 (/M is CR, /` is space; "/" and ""' have no
01AF                             ; bit 6, so // and /" give themselves).
01AF                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    H_PRINT:   LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   22h   
                              JR   Z,pr9   
                              CP   "/"   
                              JR   NZ,pr1   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              AND   0BFh   
                    PR1:      RST   28h   
                              JR   h_print   
01AF                          ENDIF      
01AF                          IF   CHECKED   
01AF                             ; (The checked build has the loop as a routine, prstr, which the error
01AF                             ; report uses too. The address is kept on the stack meanwhile: a report
01AF                             ; shows the stack as it was before the "$".)
01AF   E5           H_PRINT:   PUSH   HL   
01B0   CD 48 04               CALL   prstr   
01B3   D1                     POP   DE   
01B4   DF                     RST   18h   
01B5                          ENDIF      
01B5                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*EDITOR   
                                 ; (With the editor the loop is a routine, prstr, which ^V uses too.)
                    H_PRINT:   CALL   prstr   
                              RST   18h   
01B5                          ENDIF      
01B5   7D           H_EMIT:   LD   A,L   ; "'"
01B6   EF                     RST   28h   
01B7   DF           PR9:      RST   18h   
01B8                             ; "#" prints TOS as a signed decimal number, with no space after it.
01B8   C5           H_NUM:    PUSH   BC   
01B9   CD 93 02               CALL   psgn   
01BC   C1                     POP   BC   
01BD   DF                     RST   18h   
01BE                             ; "?" ( n -- c ) or ( -n -- addr )
01BE                             ;   n > 0: wait about n ms for a key; 0 if none came
01BE                             ;   n = 0: wait for a key
01BE                             ;   n < 0: read a line of at most -n characters, with echo. The buffer
01BE                             ;          holds 127 characters and the CR: a bigger count is taken as 127.
01BE   CB 7C        H_KEY:    BIT   7,H   
01C0   20 19                  JR   NZ,line   
01C2   1E 28        KT1:      LD   E,MSLOOP   ; one millisecond, roughly
01C4   CD 0D 03     KT2:      CALL   getk   
01C7   20 0E                  JR   NZ,kt3   
01C9   1D                     DEC   E   
01CA   20 F8                  JR   NZ,kt2   
01CC   7C                     LD   A,H   ; 0? never counts down: it waits
01CD   B5                     OR   L   
01CE   28 F2                  JR   Z,kt1   
01D0   2B                     DEC   HL   
01D1   7C                     LD   A,H   
01D2   B5                     OR   L   
01D3   20 ED                  JR   NZ,kt1   ; A = 0 if the time ran out
01D5   FE                     DB   0FEh   ; (CP n: steps over the one byte of ",")
01D6   7E           H_CFETCH:   LD   A,(HL)   ; "," shares "?"s ending: A becomes TOS
01D7   6F           KT3:      LD   L,A   
01D8   26 00                  LD   H,0   
01DA   F7                     RST   30h   
01DB                          IF   CPM   
                                 ; CP/M: BDOS 10 does the editing (the spec allows the platform's
                                 ; own line editor). It doesn't store the CR, so it is added here.
                    LINE:     LD   DE,127   ; TOS is minus the count: adding 127 carries
                              ADD   HL,DE   ;   only for 1 to 127, and leaves 127 - count
                              SBC   A,A   
                              AND   L   ; (0 for a count that is too big)
                              XOR   127   ; A = the count, 127 at most
                              LD   (LBHDR),A   
                              LD   DE,LBHDR   
                              LD   A,10   
                              CALL   bdosx   
                              LD   HL,LBHDR+1   
                              LD   A,(HL)   ; the count typed (0-127)
                              INC   L   ; HL = LINEBUF, whose low byte is 80h:
                              ADD   A,L   ;   adding the count to L can't carry
                              LD   L,A   
                              LD   (HL),13   
01DB                          ENDIF      
01DB                          IFN   CPM   
01DB                             ; Generic: Backspace takes the last character back (and is echoed as
01DB                             ; it is), CR ends (stored, not echoed), every other key is stored and
01DB                             ; echoed until the line is full. The line buffer starts at offset 80h
01DB                             ; of its page, so L alone is the place in the line: D holds the L of
01DB                             ; a full line.
01DB   11 7F 00     LINE:     LD   DE,127   ; TOS is minus the count: adding 127 carries
01DE   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ;   only for 1 to 127, and leaves 127 - count
01DF   9F                     SBC   A,A   
01E0   A5                     AND   L   ; (0 for a count that is too big)
01E1   2F                     CPL      
01E2   57                     LD   D,A   ; D = the L of a full line: 80h + count, FFh
01E3                             ;   at most
01E3   21 80 82               LD   HL,LINEBUF   
01E6   CD 0D 03     LN2:      CALL   getk   
01E9   28 FB                  JR   Z,ln2   
01EB   FE 0D                  CP   13   
01ED   28 16                  JR   Z,ln5   
01EF   FE 08                  CP   8   
01F1   28 0B                  JR   Z,ln4   
01F3   5F                     LD   E,A   
01F4   7D                     LD   A,L   
01F5   BA                     CP   D   
01F6   28 EE                  JR   Z,ln2   ; full
01F8   73                     LD   (HL),E   
01F9   2C                     INC   L   
01FA   7B                     LD   A,E   
01FB   EF           LN3:      RST   28h   
01FC   18 E8                  JR   ln2   
01FE   2D           LN4:      DEC   L   ; Backspace: one back, and echo it,
01FF   FA FB 01               JP   M,ln3   ;   unless the line was empty (L left the
0202   2C                     INC   L   ;   upper half of the page)
0203   18 E1                  JR   ln2   
0205   77           LN5:      LD   (HL),A   ; the CR
0206                          ENDIF      
0206   2E 80                  LD   L,LINEBUF & 0FFh   
0208   F7                     RST   30h   
0209                             ; =============================================================================
0209                             ;  More routines (no handler starts past this point)
0209                             ; =============================================================================
0209                             ; udiv: unsigned HL / DE (DE <= 8000h). Returns HL = quotient, DE = remainder.
0209                             ; Uses A, BC; the caller saves the IP. The dividend shifts up through A:C
0209                             ; while the quotient bits arrive at the bottom of C.
0209                             ; Dividing by 2 is one shift (the spec wants that fast).
0209   7B           UDIV:     LD   A,E   
020A   EE 02                  XOR   2   
020C   B2                     OR   D   
020D   20 07                  JR   NZ,udv0   
020F   CB 3C                  SRL   H   
0211   CB 1D                  RR   L   ; the quotient
0213   8F                     ADC   A,A   
0214   5F                     LD   E,A   ; the remainder: the bit that fell out (D is 0)
0215   C9                     RET      
0216   7C           UDV0:     LD   A,H   
0217   4D                     LD   C,L   
0218   21 00 00               LD   HL,0   
021B   06 10                  LD   B,16   
021D   CB 21        UDV1:     SLA   C   
021F   17                     RLA      
0220   ED 6A                  ADC   HL,HL   
0222   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   ; carry is clear here: the remainder
0224   30 02                  JR   NC,udv2   ;   always fits in 16 bits
0226   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ; too much: put it back, and cancel the
0227   0D                     DEC   C   ;   INC below
0228   0C           UDV2:     INC   C   ; a quotient bit
0229   10 F2                  DJNZ   udv1   
022B   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; DE = remainder
022C   67                     LD   H,A   
022D   69                     LD   L,C   ; HL = quotient
022E   C9                     RET      
022F                             ; rdnum: read decimal digits at IP into HL; IP is left on the first
022F                             ; non-digit. Values wrap at 16 bits, as the spec says.
022F   21 00 00     RDNUM:    LD   HL,0   
0232   0A           RDN1:     LD   A,(BC)   
0233   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
0235   FE 0A                  CP   10   
0237   D0                     RET   NC   
0238   03                     INC   BC   
0239   54                     LD   D,H   
023A   5D                     LD   E,L   
023B   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
023C   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
023D   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
023E   29                     ADD   HL,HL   ; HL * 10
023F   5F                     LD   E,A   
0240   16 00                  LD   D,0   
0242   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
0243   18 ED                  JR   rdn1   
0245                             ; skipstr: IP is inside a string; step past its closing quote. "/" escapes
0245                             ; the next character, so "/"" does not end it. Leaves A = 22h.
0245                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    SS0:      INC   BC   
                    SKIPSTR:   LD   A,(BC)   
                              INC   BC   
                              CP   "/"   
                              JR   Z,ss0   
                              CP   22h   
                              JR   NZ,skipstr   
                              RET      
0245                          ENDIF      
0245                          IF   CHECKED   
0245                             ; The checked build never steps over a NUL: if the text runs out first it
0245                             ; returns A = 0 with the IP on the NUL.
0245   0A           SKIPSTR:   LD   A,(BC)   
0246   B7                     OR   A   
0247   C8                     RET   Z   
0248   03                     INC   BC   
0249   FE 22                  CP   22h   
024B   C8                     RET   Z   
024C   FE 2F                  CP   "/"   
024E   20 F5                  JR   NZ,skipstr   
0250   0A                     LD   A,(BC)   ; the escaped character
0251   B7                     OR   A   
0252   C8                     RET   Z   
0253   03                     INC   BC   
0254   18 EF                  JR   skipstr   
0256                          ENDIF      
0256                             ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return A = 0 if it
0256                             ; was ")" and 2 if it was "]". Brackets of both kinds count together;
0256                             ; strings are stepped over whole. A NUL first ends the program (for "\" with
0256                             ; no closer; anything else that runs into the NUL had unbalanced brackets
0256                             ; anyway). D counts the open levels, starting at 1 for the one we are in:
0256                             ; skip sets it to 0 and falls through the INC that an opener comes back to.
0256                             ; 
0256                             ; The checked build also looks at the character the skip was started by,
0256                             ; which is always the one just before where it starts: "(" must end at ")",
0256                             ; "[" at "]", and neither may run into the NUL (N); a string with no closing
0256                             ; quote counts as running into it. "\" takes either closer. IX keeps the
0256                             ; place where the skip started, for the report.
0256                SKIP:        
0256                          IF   CHECKED   
0256   C5                     PUSH   BC   
0257   DD E1                  POP   IX   
0259   0B                     DEC   BC   
025A   0A                     LD   A,(BC)   
025B   03                     INC   BC   
025C   5F                     LD   E,A   ; E = the opener: ( [ or \
025D                          ENDIF      
025D   16 00                  LD   D,0   
025F   14           SK3:      INC   D   ; an opener: one deeper
0260   0A           SK1:      LD   A,(BC)   
0261                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              INC   BC   
                              OR   A   
                              JP   Z,SKEND   ; (the end of the program)
0261                          ENDIF      
0261                          IF   CHECKED   
0261   B7                     OR   A   
0262   28 22                  JR   Z,sk6   ; (the IP stays on the NUL)
0264   03                     INC   BC   
0265                          ENDIF      
0265   FE 22                  CP   22h   
0267   CC 45 02               CALL   Z,skipstr   ; leaves A = 22h, which matches nothing below
026A   D6 28                  SUB   "("   ;   (or 0, and then the NUL is read next)
026C   28 F1                  JR   Z,sk3   
026E   3D                     DEC   A   ; ")"
026F   28 08                  JR   Z,sk4   
0271   D6 32                  SUB   "["-")"   
0273   28 EA                  JR   Z,sk3   
0275   FE 02                  CP   "]"-"["   
0277   20 E7                  JR   NZ,sk1   
0279   15           SK4:      DEC   D   
027A                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              RET   Z   ; the closer at this level
                              JR   sk1   
027A                          ENDIF      
027A                          IF   CHECKED   
027A   20 E4                  JR   NZ,sk1   
027C   57                     LD   D,A   ; the closer at this level: 0 or 2. Bit 1 of the
027D   AB                     XOR   E   ;   opener is 0 for "(" and 1 for "[", and only
027E   E6 06                  AND   6   ;   "\" has bit 2: so this is 2 for the wrong
0280   FE 02                  CP   2   ;   closer, and only then
0282   7A                     LD   A,D   
0283   C0                     RET   NZ   
0284   18 05                  JR   sk7   
0286   CB 53        SK6:      BIT   2,E   ; the text ran out:
0288   C2 B2 04               JP   NZ,SKEND   ;   "\" with no closer ends the program
028B   DD E5        SK7:      PUSH   IX   ; N. The place is the opener
028D   C1                     POP   BC   
028E   3E 4E                  LD   A,"N"   
0290   C3 77 03               JP   errp   ; (errp drops skip's return address)
0293                          ENDIF      
0293                             ; psgn: print HL as a signed number. Uses BC.
0293   CB 7C        PSGN:     BIT   7,H   
0295   28 04                  JR   Z,pdec   
0297   3E 2D                  LD   A,"-"   
0299   EF                     RST   28h   
029A   E7                     RST   20h   
029B                             ; pdec: print HL unsigned, by recursion on HL / 10 (the stack holds digits).
029B                             ; Uses BC.
029B   11 0A 00     PDEC:     LD   DE,10   
029E   CD 09 02               CALL   udiv   ; HL = HL / 10, E = the last digit
02A1   7B                     LD   A,E   
02A2   F5                     PUSH   AF   
02A3   7C                     LD   A,H   
02A4   B5                     OR   L   
02A5   C4 9B 02               CALL   NZ,pdec   
02A8   F1                     POP   AF   
02A9   C6 30                  ADD   A,"0"   
02AB   EF                     RST   28h   
02AC   C9                     RET      
02AD                             ; =============================================================================
02AD                             ;  Dispatch table: the low byte of each handler's address, in code order
02AD                             ;  (the table itself is the macro PTABLE, defined above the dispatcher).
02AD                             ;  It must not cross a page (the dispatcher only adds to its low byte).
02AD                             ; =============================================================================
02AD                             ; The handlers of the first NPG1 characters start in the image's second page.
02AD                             ; ] \ [ @ sit where the two pages meet, and which side each lands on
02AD                             ; differs between the builds, so the count is worked out here.
02AD                             ; (One division to a line: asm80 only rounds down when it stores a value.)
02AD                PGRET:    EQU   (h_ret-BASE)/256   ; 0 = first page, 1 = second
02AD                PGBRK:    EQU   (h_break-BASE)/256   
02AD                PGDEF:    EQU   (h_def-BASE)/256   
02AD                PGFET:    EQU   (h_fetch-BASE)/256   
02AD                NPG1:     EQU   21 + PGFET + PGDEF + PGBRK + PGRET   
02AD                          IF   1-TABP0   
02AD                PTAB:        
02AD                          ;*Macro unroll:  PTABLE
02AD   9C                     DB   h_store & 0FFh   
02AE   A4                     DB   h_str & 0FFh   
02AF   B8                     DB   h_num & 0FFh   
02B0   AF                     DB   h_print & 0FFh   
02B1   94                     DB   h_swap & 0FFh   
02B2   37                     DB   h_and & 0FFh   
02B3   B5                     DB   h_emit & 0FFh   
02B4   13                     DB   h_open & 0FFh   
02B5   1B                     DB   h_close & 0FFh   
02B6   58                     DB   h_mul & 0FFh   
02B7   2E                     DB   h_add & 0FFh   
02B8   D6                     DB   h_cfetch & 0FFh   
02B9   26                     DB   h_sub & 0FFh   
02BA   96                     DB   h_cstore & 0FFh   
02BB   6C                     DB   h_div & 0FFh   
02BC   92                     DB   h_dup & 0FFh   
02BD   9B                     DB   h_drop & 0FFh   
02BE   3F                     DB   h_lt & 0FFh   
02BF   4E                     DB   h_eq & 0FFh   
02C0   40                     DB   h_gt & 0FFh   
02C1   BE                     DB   h_key & 0FFh   
02C2   0E                     DB   h_fetch & 0FFh   
02C3   EA                     DB   h_def & 0FFh   
02C4   DD                     DB   h_break & 0FFh   
02C5   D9                     DB   h_ret & 0FFh   
02C6   72                     DB   h_xor & 0FFh   
02C7   85                     DB   h_alloc & 0FFh   
02C8   C3                     DB   h_grave & 0FFh   
02C9   2C                     DB   h_tor & 0FFh   
02CA   7A                     DB   h_or & 0FFh   
02CB   1C                     DB   h_fromr & 0FFh   
02CC   82                     DB   h_not & 0FFh   
02CD                PTABEND:      
02CD                          ENDIF      
02CD                             ; hexc: if the character at IP is a hex digit (0-9, A-F, a-f), step over it
02CD                             ; and return its value in A with the carry set; otherwise leave the IP and
02CD                             ; return with the carry clear.
02CD   0A           HEXC:     LD   A,(BC)   
02CE   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
02D0   FE 0A                  CP   10   
02D2   38 09                  JR   C,hc1   
02D4   E6 DF                  AND   0DFh   
02D6   D6 11                  SUB   11h   
02D8   FE 06                  CP   6   
02DA   D0                     RET   NC   
02DB   D6 F6                  SUB   0F6h   ; + 10, and sets the carry
02DD   03           HC1:      INC   BC   
02DE   C9                     RET      
02DF                             ; =============================================================================
02DF                             ;  Console layer. rawk is the host's key routine: a waiting key in A (zero
02DF                             ;  flag clear), or A = 0 with the zero flag set when none is waiting. putc
02DF                             ;  (RST 28h) prints A. Both keep BC, DE, HL and HL'. In the generic build
02DF                             ;  they are the host's KEY and CONOUT routines themselves.
02DF                             ; 
02DF                             ;  A running program reads the keyboard only through getk and pollk, which
02DF                             ;  between them give the break key its rules:
02DF                             ;    - Ctrl-C stops the program;
02DF                             ;    - any other key that the break check reads is held in KEYBUF for the
02DF                             ;      next "?", and a newer one takes its place;
02DF                             ;    - "?" (getk) takes the held key first;
02DF                             ;    - a program that has stored a non-zero byte at BRKOFF gets Ctrl-C as a
02DF                             ;      key like any other, but two of them within about 250 ms still stop it.
02DF                             ;  Both are called straight from a handler, never from a routine under one:
02DF                             ;  the checked build's report counts on finding one return address above the
02DF                             ;  data stack.
02DF                             ; =============================================================================
02DF                          IFN   CPM   
02DF                RAWK:     EQU   KEY   
02DF                          ENDIF      
02DF                             ; pollk: the break check (see rpushn).
02DF   CD 06 FF     POLLK:    CALL   rawk   
02E2   C8                     RET   Z   ; no key
02E3   32 7A 82               LD   (KEYBUF),A   ; held for the next "?"
02E6   FE 03        PK1:      CP   3   ; (getk joins here)
02E8   C0                     RET   NZ   
02E9                             ; ctlc: Ctrl-C has been read. If the break key is on, that is the end. If
02E9                             ; the program has turned it off, wait about 250 ms for one more key: a
02E9                             ; second Ctrl-C is the end too; any other key is held (the newest wins),
02E9                             ; and the Ctrl-C goes to the program: returns A = 3, zero flag clear.
02E9   3A 7B 82     CTLC:     LD   A,(BRKOFF)   
02EC   B7                     OR   A   
02ED   CA 75 03     CT0:      JP   Z,brk   
02F0   D5                     PUSH   DE   
02F1   11 10 27               LD   DE,250*MSLOOP   
02F4   CD 06 FF     CT1:      CALL   rawk   
02F7   20 05                  JR   NZ,ct2   
02F9   1B                     DEC   DE   
02FA   7A                     LD   A,D   
02FB   B3                     OR   E   
02FC   20 F6                  JR   NZ,ct1   
02FE   D1           CT2:      POP   DE   ; A = the second key, or 0 if none came
02FF   FE 03                  CP   3   
0301   28 EA                  JR   Z,ct0   ; (the zero flag takes the JP there)
0303   B7                     OR   A   
0304   28 03                  JR   Z,ct3   
0306   32 7A 82               LD   (KEYBUF),A   
0309   3E 03        CT3:      LD   A,3   
030B   B7                     OR   A   
030C   C9                     RET      
030D                             ; getk: a key for "?", or A = 0 and the zero flag if there is none.
030D   E5           GETK:     PUSH   HL   ; a held key goes first, and is taken out of
030E   21 7A 82               LD   HL,KEYBUF   ;   the buffer
0311   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
0312   36 00                  LD   (HL),0   
0314   E1                     POP   HL   
0315   B7                     OR   A   
0316   C0                     RET   NZ   
0317   CD 06 FF               CALL   rawk   
031A   C8                     RET   Z   
031B   18 C9                  JR   pk1   ; Ctrl-C? If not, that is the key
031D                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    BRK:      EQU   endprog   ; the unchecked build stops without a word
031D                          ENDIF      ;   (with the editor, both stacks are cleared);
031D                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*EDITOR   
                    BRK:      EQU   edit0   
031D                          ENDIF      
031D                          IF   CHECKED   
031D                BRK:      EQU   e_break   ;   the checked build reports B
031D                          ENDIF      
031D                          IF   CPM   
                    RAWK:     LD   A,0FFh   ; BDOS 6 with E = FFh: a key, or 0
                                 ; putc: BDOS 6 for every character. BDOS 2 would check for ^S while
                                 ; printing and could swallow a key that BDOS 6 then never sees.
                    PUTC:     PUSH   DE   
                              PUSH   HL   
                              LD   E,A   
                              LD   A,6   
                              CALL   bdosx   
                              POP   HL   
                              POP   DE   
                              OR   A   ; (for getk)
                              RET      
                                 ; bdosx: call BDOS function A with DE, keeping BC and HL'
                    BDOSX:    PUSH   BC   
                              EXX      
                              PUSH   HL   
                              EXX      
                              LD   C,A   
                              CALL   BDOS   
                              EXX      
                              POP   HL   
                              EXX      
                              POP   BC   
                              RET      
031D                          ENDIF      
031D                             ; =============================================================================
031D                             ;  Checked build: the checks and the error report
031D                             ; =============================================================================
031D                          IF   CHECKED   
031D                             ; chkstk: both stacks are checked once per character, not in every handler.
031D                             ; The data stack is right when SP lies in the 256 bytes below DSTOP: adding
031D                             ; the constant carries if it is above (cells were popped that were never
031D                             ; pushed), and leaves a high byte of FFh if it is in range. Errors are found
031D                             ; a character late at most: the bytes above DSTOP and the guard band below
031D                             ; the page take what happens meanwhile. DE is free between characters.
031D   EB           CHKSTK:   EX   DE,HL   
031E   21 05 7E               LD   HL,(1-DSTOP)&0FFFFh   ; (SP is 2 lower here: the call)
0321   39                     ADD   HL,SP   
0322   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0323   38 1D                  JR   C,e_under   
0325   14                     INC   D   
0326   20 16                  JR   NZ,e_over   
0328   D9                     EXX      ; the return stack: in its page (or it has
0329   7C                     LD   A,H   ;   overflowed), and not above its empty
032A   FE 80                  CP   RSPAGE   ;   position (an underflow stays inside the
032C   7D                     LD   A,L   ;   page, in the guard band)
032D   D9                     EXX      
032E   20 0B                  JR   NZ,e_rover   
0330   FE E1                  CP   RSTOP&0FFh+1   
0332   D8                     RET   C   
0333   D9                     EXX      ; return stack underflow: it counts as empty
0334   2E E0                  LD   L,RSTOP&0FFh   ;   (H is right: the pointer is in its page)
0336   D9                     EXX      
0337   3E 72                  LD   A,"r"   
0339   18 3C                  JR   errp   
033B   3E 52        E_ROVER:   LD   A,"R"   ; return stack overflow
033D   11                     DB   11h   ; (LD DE,nn hides the next entry)
033E   3E 53        E_OVER:   LD   A,"S"   ; data stack overflow
0340   18 35                  JR   errp   
0342   31 FC 81     E_UNDER:   LD   SP,DSTOP   ; data stack underflow: it counts as empty
0345   3E 73                  LD   A,"s"   
0347   18 3E                  JR   error   
0349                             ; e_hi: the inner loop read a reserved byte, 80h-FFh: X. But a word cell that
0349                             ; was never defined still holds 0000h, and the byte there is a reserved one
0349                             ; in every build (AFh or C3h): if the IP is in page zero, this was a call of
0349                             ; an undefined word. The call is undone, so the place is the call itself.
0349   04           E_HI:     INC   B   
034A   10 33                  DJNZ   e_resv   ; (B is as it was, and is not 0)
034C   CF                     RST   08h   
034D   42                     LD   B,D   
034E   4B                     LD   C,E   
034F   3E 55                  LD   A,"U"   
0351   18 34                  JR   error   
0353                             ; chkhp: HL = the new heap top, DE = the old one, the carry is from adding
0353                             ; the count. Stop if the top is not below the limit page, or is below the
0353                             ; program's end.
0353                CHKHP:       
0353                          ENDIF      
0353                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
                                 ; With this much room a top that wrapped round can land back in
                                 ; range, so the add is tested too: growing (A, the count's high
                                 ; byte, is positive) must not carry, and releasing must.
                              RRA      ; the carry comes in above the sign:
                              ADD   A,40h   ;   bit 7 = carry XOR sign
                              ADD   A,A   
                              JR   C,e_heap   
                              LD   A,(0007h)   
                              DEC   A   
                              CP   H   
                              JR   C,e_heap   
0353                          ENDIF      
0353                          IF   CHECKED*(1-CPM)   
0353                             ; (Here the program's space is under 32K, so a top that wrapped
0353                             ; round always falls outside it.)
0353   7C                     LD   A,H   
0354   FE F0                  CP   HEAPLIM   
0356   30 09                  JR   NC,e_heap   
0358                          ENDIF      
0358                          IF   CHECKED   
0358   D5                     PUSH   DE   
0359   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
035A   2A 38 82               LD   HL,(NPEND)   
035D   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ; carry: at or above the program's end
035E   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
035F   D1                     POP   DE   
0360   D8                     RET   C   
0361   B7           E_HEAP:   OR   A   ; put the count back in TOS for the report
0362   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   
0364   3E 48                  LD   A,"H"   
0366   18 0F                  JR   errp   
0368                             ; chkst: stop unless HL is in the program's own space: from the letter page
0368                             ; up to the heap limit (the OS, or HEAPLIM), so the interpreter's stacks and
0368                             ; whatever lies above the limit are safe. Memory above the heap top but
0368                             ; below the limit is the program's own: Tiny BASIC keeps its lines there.
0368                             ; It is the page of HL + 1 that is tested, so that one test serves both
0368                             ; bytes of a cell: the last byte below the limit can"t be stored to with ".'.
0368                             ; Keeps HL and BC. It runs on into its own error entry.
0368   23           CHKST:    INC   HL   
0369   7C                     LD   A,H   
036A   2B                     DEC   HL   
036B   FE 82                  CP   LETPAGE   
036D   38 03                  JR   C,e_store   
036F                          ENDIF      
036F                          IF   CHECKED*(1-CPM)   
036F   FE F0                  CP   HEAPLIM   
0371   D8                     RET   C   
0372                          ENDIF      
0372                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
                              LD   E,A   
                              LD   A,(0007h)   ; the BDOS page is the heap limit
                              DEC   A   
                              CP   E   
                              RET   NC   
0372                          ENDIF      
0372                          IF   CHECKED   
0372                             ; Error entries. Each loads its letter and then hides the next entry inside
0372                             ; a 3-byte LD DE,nn (the 11h), so they all fall through to `error`.
0372   3E 4F        E_STORE:   LD   A,"O"   ; a store outside the program's space
0374   11                     DB   11h   
0375   3E 42        E_BREAK:   LD   A,"B"   ; Ctrl-C (found inside pollk or getk)
0377                             ; errp: an error found inside a routine: drop its return address first.
0377   D1           ERRP:     POP   DE   
0378   18 0D                  JR   error   
037A   44           E_QUOTE:   LD   B,H   ; an unclosed string: HL is its address, one
037B   4D                     LD   C,L   ;   past the opening quote, which is the place
037C   3E 51                  LD   A,"Q"   
037E   11                     DB   11h   
037F   3E 58        E_RESV:   LD   A,"X"   ; a reserved byte outside a string
0381   11                     DB   11h   
0382   3E 5A        E_ZERO:   LD   A,"Z"   ; dividing by zero
0384   11                     DB   11h   
0385   3E 57        E_BRACK:   LD   A,"W"   ; bad character after [
0387                             ; error: the report, then the end. A = the letter, BC = one past the place,
0387                             ; HL = TOS, and both stacks as the report is to show them:
0387                             ; 
0387                             ;   Err X @ line,col
0387                             ;   up to 16 characters of the text from the place
0387                             ;   Stk n: the top 8 cells at most, bottom to top
0387                             ;   Rtn n
0387   E5           ERROR:    PUSH   HL   ; now the whole data stack is in memory
0388   5F                     LD   E,A   
0389   CD 5B 04               CALL   pnl   
038C   45 72 72 20 22         DB   "Err ",22h   
0391   7B                     LD   A,E   
0392   EF                     RST   28h   
0393   CD 61 04               CALL   pmsg   
0396   20 40 20 22            DB   " @ ",22h   
039A   0B                     DEC   BC   ; BC = the place
039B                             ; The line and column. A place below the program is in the line
039B                             ; buffer: line 0. Otherwise count the LFs from the program's start;
039B                             ; DE = the line's number, HL = where it starts.
039B   21 80 82               LD   HL,LINEBUF   
039E   11 00 00               LD   DE,0   
03A1   78                     LD   A,B   
03A2   FE 83                  CP   PROG/256   
03A4   38 14                  JR   C,er3   
03A6   24                     INC   H   
03A7   6B                     LD   L,E   ; HL = PROG
03A8   13           ER1:      INC   DE   ; a new line starts at HL
03A9   E5                     PUSH   HL   
03AA   7D           ER2:      LD   A,L   
03AB   91                     SUB   C   
03AC   7C                     LD   A,H   
03AD   98                     SBC   A,B   
03AE   30 09                  JR   NC,er2x   ; reached the place
03B0   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
03B1   23                     INC   HL   
03B2   FE 0A                  CP   10   
03B4   20 F4                  JR   NZ,er2   
03B6   F1                     POP   AF   
03B7   18 EF                  JR   er1   
03B9   E1           ER2X:     POP   HL   
03BA   C5           ER3:      PUSH   BC   
03BB   E5                     PUSH   HL   
03BC   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
03BD   CD 9B 02               CALL   pdec   ; the line
03C0   3E 2C                  LD   A,","   
03C2   EF                     RST   28h   
03C3   D1                     POP   DE   
03C4   E1                     POP   HL   
03C5   E5                     PUSH   HL   
03C6   B7                     OR   A   
03C7   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   
03C9   23                     INC   HL   
03CA   CD 9B 02               CALL   pdec   ; the column
03CD   CD 5B 04               CALL   pnl   
03D0   22                     DB   22h   
03D1   E1                     POP   HL   ; the text, as it is: 16 characters, or fewer
03D2   06 10                  LD   B,16   ;   if the line or the program ends first
03D4   7E           ER4:      LD   A,(HL)   
03D5   23                     INC   HL   
03D6   B7                     OR   A   
03D7   28 0B                  JR   Z,er5   
03D9   FE 0D                  CP   13   
03DB   28 07                  JR   Z,er5   
03DD   FE 0A                  CP   10   
03DF   28 03                  JR   Z,er5   
03E1                          ENDIF      
03E1                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
                              CP   1Ah   ; (the ^Z that pads a file's last record ends
                              JR   Z,er5   ;   the text too: some terminals clear the
03E1                          ENDIF      ;   screen on it)
03E1                          IF   CHECKED   
03E1   EF                     RST   28h   
03E2   10 F0                  DJNZ   er4   
03E4                ER5:         ; (without the editor: on into pstk)
03E4                          ENDIF      
03E4                          IF   CHECKED*EDITOR   
03E4   CD EE 03               CALL   pstk   
03E7   CD 5B 04               CALL   pnl   
03EA   22                     DB   22h   
03EB   C3 AE 04               JP   edit0   ; back to the editor, with both stacks cleared
03EE                          ENDIF      
03EE                             ; =============================================================================
03EE                             ;  Routines that the checked build's report and the editor share
03EE                             ; =============================================================================
03EE                SPADJ:    EQU   2*EDITOR   ; (with the editor pstk is called, not fallen
03EE                             ;   into: the stack is one address deeper)
03EE                          IF   CHECKED+EDITOR   
03EE                             ; pstk: the two stack lines:  Stk n: the top 8 cells at most, bottom to top
03EE                             ;                             Rtn n
03EE                             ; TOS must be in memory with the rest (pushed). In a build without the
03EE                             ; editor this is the end of `error`, which runs on into it.
03EE   CD 5B 04     PSTK:     CALL   pnl   
03F1   53 74 6B 20 22         DB   "Stk ",22h   
03F6   21 08 7E               LD   HL,(2+SPADJ-DSTOP)&0FFFFh   ; SP - (DSTOP-2) is minus twice the
03F9   39                     ADD   HL,SP   ;   depth (the cell at DSTOP-2 was pushed
03FA   E7                     RST   20h   ;   with the first value and holds nothing)
03FB   CD 3E 04               CALL   phalf   ; the depth
03FE   3E 3A                  LD   A,":"   
0400   EF                     RST   28h   
0401   79                     LD   A,C   
0402   FE 09                  CP   9   
0404   38 0A                  JR   C,er6   
0406   CD 61 04               CALL   pmsg   
0409   20 2E 2E 2E 22         DB   " ...",22h   
040E   0E 08                  LD   C,8   
0410   26 00        ER6:      LD   H,0   ; C = the number of cells to show
0412   69                     LD   L,C   
0413   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
0414   39                     ADD   HL,SP   ; HL -> just above the deepest of them
0415                          ENDIF      
0415                          IF   EDITOR   
0415   23                     INC   HL   
0416   23                     INC   HL   
0417                          ENDIF      
0417                          IF   CHECKED+EDITOR   
0417   0C                     INC   C   
0418   0D           ER7:      DEC   C   
0419   28 11                  JR   Z,er8   
041B   2B                     DEC   HL   
041C   56                     LD   D,(HL)   
041D   2B                     DEC   HL   
041E   5E                     LD   E,(HL)   
041F   E5                     PUSH   HL   
0420   C5                     PUSH   BC   
0421   3E 20                  LD   A," "   
0423   EF                     RST   28h   
0424   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0425   CD 93 02               CALL   psgn   
0428   C1                     POP   BC   
0429   E1                     POP   HL   
042A   18 EC                  JR   er7   
042C   CD 5B 04     ER8:      CALL   pnl   
042F                          ENDIF      
042F                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*EDITOR   
                              DB   "Rtn 0",22h   ; (only ^V comes here, and at the editor the
                              RET      ;   return stack is always empty)
042F                          ENDIF      
042F                          IF   CHECKED   
042F   52 74 6E 20 22         DB   "Rtn ",22h   
0434   D9                     EXX      
0435   E5                     PUSH   HL   
0436   D9                     EXX      
0437   D1                     POP   DE   
0438   21 E0 80               LD   HL,RSTOP   
043B   B7                     OR   A   
043C   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   
043E                          ENDIF      
043E                          IF   CHECKED*(1-EDITOR)   
                              CALL   phalf   
                              CALL   pnl   
                              DB   22h   
                              JP   endprog   
043E                          ENDIF      
043E                          IF   CHECKED+EDITOR   
043E                             ; phalf: print half of HL, and leave it in C. (With the editor, pstk ends by
043E                             ; running on into this.)
043E   CB 3C        PHALF:    SRL   H   
0440   CB 1D                  RR   L   
0442   E5                     PUSH   HL   
0443   CD 9B 02               CALL   pdec   
0446   C1                     POP   BC   
0447   C9                     RET      
0448                             ; prstr: print the string at HL, to its closing quote, decoding "/" (this is
0448                             ; "$", and the texts of the report and the editor). In the checked build a
0448                             ; NUL first is an error: Q.
0448   7E           PRSTR:    LD   A,(HL)   
0449   23                     INC   HL   
044A   FE 22                  CP   22h   
044C   C8                     RET   Z   
044D                          ENDIF      
044D                          IF   CHECKED   
044D   B7                     OR   A   
044E   28 17                  JR   Z,e_dollar   
0450                          ENDIF      
0450                          IF   CHECKED+EDITOR   
0450   FE 2F                  CP   "/"   
0452   20 04                  JR   NZ,prs1   
0454   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
0455   23                     INC   HL   
0456   E6 BF                  AND   0BFh   
0458   EF           PRS1:     RST   28h   
0459   18 ED                  JR   prstr   
045B                             ; pmsg: print the text that follows the CALL, to its closing quote. Keeps HL.
045B                             ; pnl: the same, on a new line.
045B   3E 0D        PNL:      LD   A,13   
045D   EF                     RST   28h   
045E   3E 0A                  LD   A,10   
0460   EF                     RST   28h   
0461   E3           PMSG:     EX   (SP),HL   
0462   CD 48 04               CALL   prstr   
0465   E3                     EX   (SP),HL   
0466   C9                     RET      
0467                          ENDIF      
0467                          IF   CHECKED   
0467   D1           E_DOLLAR:   POP   DE   ; "$" ran into a NUL: drop the return address,
0468   E1                     POP   HL   ;   and put the string's address back in TOS
0469   3E 51                  LD   A,"Q"   
046B   C3 87 03               JP   error   
046E                          ENDIF      
046E                             ; =============================================================================
046E                             ;  The line editor (EDITOR = 1)
046E                             ; 
046E                             ;  The interpreter starts here, and a program that ends comes back here.
046E                             ;  There is no prompt. It follows the spec's suggested standard for a line
046E                             ;  editor (docs/b8script.md, Environments). Type a line and press Return:
046E                             ; 
046E                             ;    n text    put the text in as line n; the lines from n on move down. A
046E                             ;              number past the end (or 0) adds the line at the end.
046E                             ;    n         take line n out
046E                             ;    anything else is run at once, as B8Script. (Start such a line with a
046E                             ;    space if it would begin with a digit.)
046E                             ; 
046E                             ;  A command key ends the line too, and takes what was typed as its argument:
046E                             ; 
046E                             ;    ^G        run the program
046E                             ;    n ^L      list from line n (no number: all of it). Any key holds the
046E                             ;              list until another key is pressed; Ctrl-C ends it.
046E                             ;    n ^E      put line n in the input line; Return puts it back, changed
046E                             ;    name ^R   read. CP/M: the file of that name (no name: the same file as
046E                             ;              last time). Generic: what is typed, or pasted, from now until
046E                             ;              ^Z replaces the program; it is not echoed.
046E                             ;    name ^W   write. CP/M: to that file (no name: the same file as last
046E                             ;              time). Generic: the text is printed, as it is.
046E                             ;    ^N ^N     new: no program (the key twice in a row)
046E                             ;    ^V        view: the build, both stacks, and the program's size, lines
046E                             ;              and free memory
046E                             ;    ^X        leave (to LEAVE)
046E                             ; 
046E                             ;  In the line: ^B and ^F, or the left and right arrow keys, move the cursor;
046E                             ;  a character goes in at the cursor; Backspace and DEL take out the one
046E                             ;  before it; Esc drops the line. Only CR, LF, BS and printing characters are
046E                             ;  sent to the terminal, so any terminal will do.
046E                             ; 
046E                             ;  Lines are counted, not numbered: the text holds no line numbers, and the
046E                             ;  list shows each line's place. There can be 65535 lines. A typed line holds
046E                             ;  125 characters; the one character after a line number separates it from
046E                             ;  the text and is not stored. The text is kept as it is typed, each line
046E                             ;  ending in CR LF, at PROG.
046E                             ; 
046E                             ;  What lasts from one line to the next: the program, the words, the
046E                             ;  variables and the data stack. An error or a break clears both stacks. The
046E                             ;  return stack starts empty for every line.
046E                             ; 
046E                             ;  Things to know:
046E                             ;    - Reset empties the program (generic builds).
046E                             ;    - A word's address points into the program, so run the program again
046E                             ;      after editing it.
046E                             ;    - Nothing is printed between a program's output and what is typed next.
046E                             ;    - A line run at once sits in the line buffer, which -n? also reads into:
046E                             ;      a line that calls -n? and carries on afterwards runs what was typed.
046E                             ;      (The stored program never comes back to the line, so it may.)
046E                             ;    - The editor"s own keys are not the program"s: -n? is the plain line
046E                             ;      read of the other builds (BDOS 10 under CP/M).
046E                             ; 
046E                             ;  The data stack is the CPU's stack, so the editor works on top of whatever
046E                             ;  the last line left there, with TOS pushed like the rest.
046E                             ; =============================================================================
046E                          IF   EDGEN   
046E                INIT:        ; reset (A = 0)
046E                          ENDIF      
046E                          IF   EDGEN*CHECKED   
046E                             ; Clear the lower half of the letter page: every variable starts at 0, and
046E                             ; every word cell holds 0000h, the address an undefined word is caught at
046E                             ; (see e_hi).
046E   21 00 82               LD   HL,LET   
0471   77           INI1:     LD   (HL),A   
0472   2C                     INC   L   
0473   F2 71 04               JP   P,ini1   ; +00h to +7Fh
0476                          ENDIF      
0476                          IF   EDGEN   
0476   18 36                  JR   edit0   
0478                          ENDIF      
0478                          IF   EDITOR   
0478                             ; ^F, right arrow: one to the right, by printing the character there
0478   7D           RIGHT:    LD   A,L   
0479   BB                     CP   E   
047A   28 4A                  JR   Z,ed1   ; at the end
047C   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
047D   2C                     INC   L   
047E   18 2B                  JR   lf1   
0480                             ; Esc: alone it drops the line. An arrow key sends Esc [ and a letter, so
0480                             ; wait about 5 ms for a second key: after a "[" read on to the letter that
0480                             ; ends the sequence, and act on C (right) and D (left).
0480   01 C8 00     ESC:      LD   BC,5*MSLOOP   
0483   CD 06 FF     ES1:      CALL   rawk   
0486   20 0A                  JR   NZ,es2   
0488   0B                     DEC   BC   
0489   78                     LD   A,B   
048A   B1                     OR   C   
048B   20 F6                  JR   NZ,es1   
048D   CD FB 04               CALL   fin   ; no second key: the line is dropped
0490   18 22                  JR   edit   
0492   FE 5B        ES2:      CP   "["   
0494   20 30                  JR   NZ,ed1   ; not a sequence known here
0496   CD 54 05     ES3:      CALL   ekey   
0499   FE 40                  CP   40h   
049B   38 F9                  JR   C,es3   ; (its parameters)
049D   D6 43                  SUB   "C"   
049F   28 D7                  JR   Z,right   
04A1   3D                     DEC   A   ; "D"?
04A2   20 22                  JR   NZ,ed1   ; no: on into left
04A4                             ; ^B, left arrow: the cursor goes one to the left
04A4   7D           LEFT:     LD   A,L   
04A5   87                     ADD   A,A   
04A6   28 1E                  JR   Z,ed1   ; (L = 80h: at the start)
04A8   2D                     DEC   L   
04A9   3E 08                  LD   A,8   
04AB   EF           LF1:      RST   28h   
04AC   18 18                  JR   ed1   
04AE                             ; edit0: reset, an error or a break: both stacks are cleared.
04AE                             ; skend: a program that ended inside skip: its return address goes.
04AE                             ; edend: a program that ended: TOS joins the rest of the data stack.
04AE   31 FA 81     EDIT0:    LD   SP,DSTOP-2   ; empty (the cell that stands for TOS is pushed)
04B1   21                     DB   21h   ; (LD HL,nn: steps over the next two bytes)
04B2   D1           SKEND:    POP   DE   
04B3   E5           EDEND:    PUSH   HL   
04B4                             ; edit: start a new input line.
04B4   D9           EDIT:     EXX      
04B5   21 E0 80               LD   HL,RSTOP   ; the return stack is empty
04B8   D9                     EXX      
04B9   21 00 00               LD   HL,0   
04BC   22 7A 82               LD   (KEYBUF),HL   ; no key is held, and the break key is on
04BF   22 3A 82               LD   (EDLN),HL   ; no line is being edited
04C2   21 80 82               LD   HL,LINEBUF   ; HL = the cursor,
04C5   5D                     LD   E,L   ;   E = the end of the line (its low byte)
04C6   CD 54 05     ED1:      CALL   ekey   
04C9   FE 7F                  CP   7Fh   
04CB   28 40                  JR   Z,bsp   ; DEL
04CD   FE 20                  CP   " "   
04CF   30 56                  JR   NC,insc   
04D1   FE 09                  CP   9   
04D3   28 52                  JR   Z,insc   ; Tab is text
04D5   FE 08                  CP   8   
04D7   28 34                  JR   Z,bsp   
04D9   FE 02                  CP   2   
04DB   28 C7                  JR   Z,left   ; ^B
04DD   FE 06                  CP   6   
04DF   28 97                  JR   Z,right   ; ^F
04E1   FE 1B                  CP   1Bh   
04E3   28 9B                  JR   Z,esc   
04E5   E5                     PUSH   HL   ; a command key? Look it up
04E6   21 5A 05               LD   HL,cmds   
04E9   06 09                  LD   B,NCMD   
04EB   BE           ED2:      CP   (HL)   
04EC   23                     INC   HL   
04ED   28 07                  JR   Z,ed3   
04EF   23                     INC   HL   
04F0   23                     INC   HL   
04F1   10 F8                  DJNZ   ed2   
04F3   E1                     POP   HL   
04F4   18 D0                  JR   ed1   ; no: the key is ignored
04F6   7E           ED3:      LD   A,(HL)   
04F7   23                     INC   HL   
04F8   66                     LD   H,(HL)   
04F9   6F                     LD   L,A   
04FA   E3                     EX   (SP),HL   ; the command's address: fin returns to it
04FB                             ; fin: end the input line: CR LF and a NUL after it, and a new line on the
04FB                             ; terminal. Leaves BC -> the line and HL -> the NUL.
04FB   26 82        FIN:      LD   H,LETPAGE   
04FD   6B                     LD   L,E   
04FE   36 0D                  LD   (HL),13   
0500   2C                     INC   L   
0501   36 0A                  LD   (HL),10   
0503   2D                     DEC   L   
0504   CD C3 06               CALL   prl   ; (prints the CR LF)
0507   36 00                  LD   (HL),0   
0509   01 80 82               LD   BC,LINEBUF   
050C   C9                     RET      
050D                             ; Backspace, DEL: the character before the cursor goes. The cursor moves
050D                             ; left, the rest of the line moves down over it, and the last place (now a
050D                             ; space) is printed over along with the rest.
050D   7D           BSP:      LD   A,L   
050E   87                     ADD   A,A   
050F   28 B5                  JR   Z,ed1   ; at the start
0511   2D                     DEC   L   
0512   3E 08                  LD   A,8   
0514   EF                     RST   28h   
0515   E5                     PUSH   HL   
0516   2C           BS1:      INC   L   
0517   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
0518   2D                     DEC   L   
0519   77                     LD   (HL),A   
051A   2C                     INC   L   
051B   7D                     LD   A,L   
051C   BB                     CP   E   
051D   20 F7                  JR   NZ,bs1   
051F   2D                     DEC   L   
0520   36 20                  LD   (HL)," "   
0522   E1                     POP   HL   
0523   53                     LD   D,E   
0524   1D                     DEC   E   
0525   18 15                  JR   ic2   
0527                             ; A character goes in at the cursor: it ripples up through the rest of the
0527                             ; line, the cursor moves on, and the rest is printed again.
0527   47           INSC:     LD   B,A   
0528   7B                     LD   A,E   
0529   FE FD                  CP   0FDh   
052B   28 99                  JR   Z,ed1   ; the line is full: 125 characters
052D   78                     LD   A,B   
052E   EF                     RST   28h   
052F   E5                     PUSH   HL   
0530   7E           IC1:      LD   A,(HL)   
0531   70                     LD   (HL),B   
0532   47                     LD   B,A   
0533   7D                     LD   A,L   
0534   2C                     INC   L   
0535   BB                     CP   E   
0536   20 F8                  JR   NZ,ic1   
0538   E1                     POP   HL   
0539   2C                     INC   L   
053A   1C                     INC   E   
053B   53                     LD   D,E   
053C   CD 41 05     IC2:      CALL   tail   
053F   18 85                  JR   ed1   
0541                             ; tail: print the line from the cursor to D (a low byte), and bring the
0541                             ; cursor back with backspaces. Nothing at all if the cursor is at D.
0541   4D           TAIL:     LD   C,L   
0542   7D           TA1:      LD   A,L   
0543   BA                     CP   D   
0544   28 05                  JR   Z,ta2   
0546   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
0547   EF                     RST   28h   
0548   2C                     INC   L   
0549   18 F7                  JR   ta1   
054B   7D           TA2:      LD   A,L   
054C   B9                     CP   C   
054D   C8                     RET   Z   
054E   3E 08                  LD   A,8   
0550   EF                     RST   28h   
0551   2D                     DEC   L   
0552   18 F7                  JR   ta2   
0554                             ; ekey: wait for a key
0554   CD 06 FF     EKEY:     CALL   rawk   
0557   28 FB                  JR   Z,ekey   
0559   C9                     RET      
055A                             ; The command keys, and where each goes (after fin).
055A   0D           CMDS:     DB   13   
055B   AD 05                  DW   cret   
055D   07                     DB   7   ; ^G
055E   F5 05                  DW   crun   
0560   0C                     DB   12   ; ^L
0561   0B 06                  DW   clist   
0563   05                     DB   5   ; ^E
0564   83 05                  DW   cedln   
0566   12                     DB   18   ; ^R
0567   CC 06                  DW   cread   
0569   17                     DB   23   ; ^W
056A   F9 06                  DW   cwrite   
056C   0E                     DB   14   ; ^N
056D   75 05                  DW   cnew   
056F   16                     DB   22   ; ^V
0570   3B 06                  DW   cview   
0572   18                     DB   24   ; ^X
0573   09 FF                  DW   LEAVE   
0575                NCMD:     EQU   9   
0575                             ; ^N ^N: no program, if the next key is ^N too
0575   CD 54 05     CNEW:     CALL   ekey   
0578   FE 0E                  CP   14   
057A   20 04                  JR   NZ,ged0   
057C   AF                     XOR   A   
057D   32 00 83               LD   (PROG),A   
0580   C3 B4 04     GED0:     JP   edit   
0583                             ; ^E: line n goes into the input line, to be changed. EDLN remembers which
0583                             ; line it was: Return puts the text back in its place.
0583   CD 2F 02     CEDLN:    CALL   rdnum   
0586   E5                     PUSH   HL   
0587   CD AB 06               CALL   find   ; HL -> the line, or the NUL if there is none
058A   D1                     POP   DE   
058B   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
058C   B7                     OR   A   
058D   28 F1                  JR   Z,ged0   
058F   ED 53 3A 82            LD   (EDLN),DE   
0593   11 80 82               LD   DE,LINEBUF   
0596   7E           CE1:      LD   A,(HL)   ; copy it, and show it, up to its CR (or LF)
0597   FE 0D                  CP   13   
0599   28 0D                  JR   Z,ce2   
059B   FE 0A                  CP   10   
059D   28 09                  JR   Z,ce2   
059F   12                     LD   (DE),A   
05A0   EF                     RST   28h   
05A1   23                     INC   HL   
05A2   1C                     INC   E   
05A3   7B                     LD   A,E   
05A4   FE FD                  CP   0FDh   ; (a longer line is cut at 125 characters)
05A6   20 EE                  JR   NZ,ce1   
05A8   EB           CE2:      EX   DE,HL   ; the cursor is at the line's end
05A9   5D                     LD   E,L   
05AA   C3 C6 04               JP   ed1   
05AD                             ; Return. If ^E put a line here, the text goes back in its place. If not:
05AD                             ; a number and text is a line to put in, a number alone a line to take out,
05AD                             ; and anything else is run where it is.
05AD   E5           CRET:     PUSH   HL   ; the end of what was typed
05AE   2A 3A 82               LD   HL,(EDLN)   
05B1   7C                     LD   A,H   
05B2   B5                     OR   L   
05B3   28 07                  JR   Z,cr1   
05B5   E5                     PUSH   HL   
05B6   CD 9B 06               CALL   delln   
05B9   E1                     POP   HL   
05BA   18 13                  JR   ins   
05BC   CD 2F 02     CR1:      CALL   rdnum   ; HL = the number it starts with, BC -> after
05BF   79                     LD   A,C   ; C is still 80h if there was no number:
05C0   87                     ADD   A,A   ;   only then is twice it 0
05C1   28 36                  JR   Z,st0p   ; no number: run the line
05C3   0A                     LD   A,(BC)   
05C4   FE 0D                  CP   13   
05C6   20 06                  JR   NZ,cr2   
05C8   D1                     POP   DE   ; the number alone: take that line out
05C9   CD 9B 06               CALL   delln   
05CC   18 24                  JR   gedit   
05CE   03           CR2:      INC   BC   ; step over the one character after the number
05CF                             ; Put the text at BC in as line n (in HL): open a gap of its length there,
05CF                             ; CR and LF included, and copy it in.
05CF   CD AB 06     INS:      CALL   find   ; HL -> where it goes
05D2   D1                     POP   DE   ; the end of what was typed
05D3   7B                     LD   A,E   
05D4   91                     SUB   C   ; A = the length of the text, with its CR LF
05D5   C5                     PUSH   BC   ; the text
05D6   4F                     LD   C,A   
05D7   06 00                  LD   B,0   
05D9   C5                     PUSH   BC   ; its length
05DA   54                     LD   D,H   
05DB   5D                     LD   E,L   ; DE = where it goes
05DC   AF                     XOR   A   
05DD   4F                     LD   C,A   ; BC = 0: CPIR looks as far as it needs to
05DE   ED B1                  CPIR      ; HL -> one past the program's NUL
05E0   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   ; the number of bytes to move up, NUL included
05E2   44                     LD   B,H   
05E3   4D                     LD   C,L   
05E4   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
05E5   2B                     DEC   HL   ; HL -> the NUL
05E6   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
05E7   E3                     EX   (SP),HL   ; HL = the length; where it goes is kept
05E8   E5                     PUSH   HL   
05E9   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ; the NUL's new place
05EA   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
05EB   ED B8                  LDDR      ; move the rest of the program up
05ED   C1                     POP   BC   ; the length
05EE   D1                     POP   DE   ; where it goes
05EF   E1                     POP   HL   ; the text
05F0   ED B0                  LDIR      
05F2   C3 B4 04     GEDIT:    JP   edit   
05F5                             ; ^G: run the program. st0p: run the typed line (BC -> it).
05F5   01 00 83     CRUN:     LD   BC,PROG   
05F8   3E                     DB   3Eh   ; (LD A,n: steps over the POP)
05F9   E1           ST0P:     POP   HL   ; (the end of what was typed)
05FA                             ; st0: start running at BC. The heap starts after the stored program's NUL.
05FA   21 00 83     ST0:      LD   HL,PROG   
05FD   AF                     XOR   A   
05FE   BE           ST1:      CP   (HL)   
05FF   23                     INC   HL   
0600   20 FC                  JR   NZ,st1   
0602   22 7C 82               LD   (HEAP),HL   
0605                          ENDIF      
0605                          IF   EDITOR*CHECKED   
0605   E7                     RST   20h   ; minus the heap"s first address: "_' may not
0606   22 38 82               LD   (NPEND),HL   ;   release below it
0609                          ENDIF      
0609                          IF   EDITOR   
0609   E1                     POP   HL   ; TOS: the data stack is as the last line left it
060A   F7                     RST   30h   ; (its return address is thrown away)
060B                             ; ^L: list from line n. DE = the number of the line at HL.
060B   CD 2F 02     CLIST:    CALL   rdnum   ; HL = n, or 0 if there was none:
060E   7C                     LD   A,H   
060F   B5                     OR   L   
0610   20 01                  JR   NZ,li0   
0612   2C                     INC   L   ;   then from line 1
0613   E5           LI0:      PUSH   HL   
0614   CD AB 06               CALL   find   
0617   D1                     POP   DE   
0618   7E           LI1:      LD   A,(HL)   
0619   B7                     OR   A   
061A   28 D6                  JR   Z,gedit   ; the end of the text
061C   CD 06 FF               CALL   rawk   
061F   28 09                  JR   Z,li3   ; no key: carry on
0621   FE 03                  CP   3   
0623   C4 54 05               CALL   NZ,ekey   ; any key but Ctrl-C: wait for one more
0626   FE 03                  CP   3   
0628   28 C8                  JR   Z,gedit   ; Ctrl-C, first or second, ends the list
062A   E5           LI3:      PUSH   HL   
062B   D5                     PUSH   DE   
062C   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
062D   CD 9B 02               CALL   pdec   ; the line's number,
0630   3E 20                  LD   A," "   
0632   EF                     RST   28h   ;   a space,
0633   D1                     POP   DE   
0634   E1                     POP   HL   
0635   13                     INC   DE   
0636   CD C3 06               CALL   prl   ;   and the line
0639   18 DD                  JR   li1   
063B                             ; ^V: view.
063B   CD 61 04     CVIEW:    CALL   pmsg   
063E   42 38 53 5A 38 30 45   DB   "B8SZ80E"   
0645                          ENDIF      
0645                          IF   EDITOR*CHECKED   
0645   43                     DB   "C"   
0646                          ENDIF      
0646                          IF   EDITOR   
0646   20 32 30 32 36 2D 31 31 2D 32 31 22 DB   " 2026-11-21",22h   
0652   CD EE 03               CALL   pstk   ; both stacks
0655   21 00 83               LD   HL,PROG   
0658   11 FF FF               LD   DE,0FFFFh   
065B   13           CV1:      INC   DE   ; count the lines, and find the end
065C   CD B9 06               CALL   nxl   
065F   20 FA                  JR   NZ,cv1   
